-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 25: COURT FEES (rules 1 to 8), layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT: as in roc6-order-23.l4.
--   JUST TRUE    the text says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the text says no in its own words: a definition that "means", a condition introduced by "if",
--                "where", "unless" or "only if", a flat negative ("not payable"), or a time fixed in the text's own
--                words and missed ("within one month", "within 3 months"; ruling of 2026-11-05).
--   NOTHING      the text does not answer: it is silent on what follows a failure to comply with a "must", a list is
--                not closed ("includes"), a fact lives in another Order (Order 21 Part 6 of Appendix 1, the Fourth
--                Schedule), or a grant ("may") is limited by its own wording and the case is outside the limit.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every requirement here is subject to the Court's discretion to order otherwise (O 3 r 2(1)).
-- A period is counted by Order 3, Rule 3 (roc1's range): each function takes the last day that Rule gives as the input
-- `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`.  The Fourth Schedule (roc12's range) says how much each fee is; this Order
-- says when a fee is payable, what counts as a court fee and how the value of a claim is found.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 25 -- Court fees`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- Definitions of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3927 | 1. In this Order — “Court ADR service” means a service provided by the State Courts for resolving a dispute by an alternative dispute resolution process (such as mediation or neutral evaluation);
@ref O 25 r 1 "Court ADR service" (src:3927)
GIVEN `the service is provided by the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is for resolving a dispute by an alternative dispute resolution process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 1 "Court ADR service" is a service provided by the State Courts for resolving a dispute by an alternative dispute resolution process` MEANS
    IF `the service is provided by the State Courts` AND `the service is for resolving a dispute by an alternative dispute resolution process`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Court ADR service” means a service provided by the State Courts for resolving a dispute by an alternative dispute resolution process"

DECLARE `o 25 r 1 kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `o 25 r 1 a charge, commission or fee payable under these Rules`
    `o 25 r 1(a) a document fee payable on the filing or sealing of a specified document`
    `o 25 r 1(b) a hearing fee payable for a specified hearing`
    `o 25 r 1(c) a fee for provision of a Court ADR service by the State Courts`
    `o 25 r 1(d) a service provision fee payable for a service to be provided or rendered by, or which requires the attendance of, a court officer`
    `o 25 r 1(e) a search fee payable for a search to be made of court records`
    `o 25 r 1(f) a fee relating to an admiralty matter`
    `o 25 r 1 some other payment`

-- src:3928 | “court fees” includes all charges, commissions and fees payable under these Rules, and the following: ( a )
-- src:3929 | document fees payable on the filing or sealing of specified documents;
-- src:3930 | ( b )
-- src:3931 | hearing fees payable for specified hearings;
-- src:3932 | ( c )
-- src:3933 | fees for provision of a Court ADR service by the State Courts;
-- src:3934 | ( d )
-- src:3935 | service provision fees payable for services to be provided or rendered by, or which require the attendance of, court officers;
-- src:3936 | ( e )
-- src:3937 | search fees payable for a search to be made of court records;
-- src:3938 | ( f )
-- src:3939 | fees relating to admiralty matters;
@ref O 25 r 1 "court fees" (src:3928-3939)
GIVEN payment IS A `o 25 r 1 kind of payment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 1 the payment is within court fees` MEANS
    CONSIDER payment
    WHEN `o 25 r 1 a charge, commission or fee payable under these Rules` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 1(a) a document fee payable on the filing or sealing of a specified document` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 1(b) a hearing fee payable for a specified hearing` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 1(c) a fee for provision of a Court ADR service by the State Courts` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 1(d) a service provision fee payable for a service to be provided or rendered by, or which requires the attendance of, a court officer` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 1(e) a search fee payable for a search to be made of court records` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 1(f) a fee relating to an admiralty matter` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 1 some other payment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“court fees” includes ..." does not close the list

DECLARE `o 25 r 1 kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `o 25 r 1 the Sheriff`
    `o 25 r 1 a commissioner for oaths`
    `o 25 r 1 an interpreter`
    `o 25 r 1 a clerk`
    `o 25 r 1 a process server`
    `o 25 r 1 a bailiff`
    `o 25 r 1 another officer attached to the court for the administration of justice and due execution of powers and duties vested in the court`
    `o 25 r 1 someone else`

-- src:3940 | “court officer” includes the Sheriff, a commissioner for oaths, interpreter, clerk, process server, bailiff or other officer attached to the court for the administration of justice and due execution of powers and duties vested in the court.
@ref O 25 r 1 "court officer" (src:3940)
GIVEN person IS A `o 25 r 1 kind of person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 1 the person is a court officer` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN `o 25 r 1 the Sheriff` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 1 a commissioner for oaths` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 1 an interpreter` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 1 a clerk` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 1 a process server` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 1 a bailiff` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 1 another officer attached to the court for the administration of justice and due execution of powers and duties vested in the court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 1 someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“court officer” includes ..." does not close the list

