-- src:3942 | 2. —(1) Court fees must be paid in the circumstances and the manner set out in this Order and in the Fourth Schedule. (2) Subject to paragraph (5), for the purpose of determining the appropriate court fees payable in the Supreme Court in the Fourth Schedule, the following apply: ( a )
@ref O 25 r 2(1) (src:3942)
GIVEN `the court fees are paid in the circumstances and the manner set out in Order 25 and the Fourth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 2(1) court fees are paid in the circumstances and the manner set out` MEANS
    IF `the court fees are paid in the circumstances and the manner set out in Order 25 and the Fourth Schedule`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says court fees "must be paid" as set out and does not say what follows if they are not

-- Paragraph (2) is "for the purpose of determining the appropriate court fees payable in the Supreme Court": a scope limit with no "only".
@ref O 25 r 2(2) (src:3942)
GIVEN establishment IS A `Court system`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 2(2) paragraph (2) applies to the court fees` MEANS
    CONSIDER establishment
    WHEN `Supreme Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `State Courts` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "payable in the Supreme Court"; the paragraph does not say how the value is found in the State Courts

-- Paragraph (4): a claim in foreign currency is converted at the exchange rate applicable as at the date of the filing of the originating process.
-- src:3953 | (4) Where the claim includes or consists of a claim in foreign currency, the value of the claim is computed after converting the claim to Singapore dollars at an exchange rate applicable as at the date of the filing of the originating process.
@ref O 25 r 2(4) (src:3953)
GIVEN `the claim is in foreign currency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the claim` IS A NUMBER
      `the exchange rate applicable as at the date of the filing of the originating process, in Singapore dollars for one unit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 25 r 2(4) the amount of the claim in Singapore dollars` MEANS
    IF `the claim is in foreign currency`
    THEN `the amount of the claim` TIMES `the exchange rate applicable as at the date of the filing of the originating process, in Singapore dollars for one unit`
    ELSE `the amount of the claim`

-- Paragraph (6): the value of the claim excludes non-contractual interest.
-- src:3955 | (6) For the purpose of this Rule, the value of the claim excludes non‑contractual interest.
@ref O 25 r 2(6) (src:3955)
GIVEN `the amount of the claim including non-contractual interest` IS A NUMBER
      `the non-contractual interest` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 25 r 2(6) the amount counted towards the value of the claim` MEANS
    `the amount of the claim including non-contractual interest` MINUS `the non-contractual interest`

-- Paragraphs (2)(a) to (e) and (3).  The amounts are in Singapore dollars, converted by paragraph (4) and net of
-- non-contractual interest by paragraph (6).  Fork F-O25-1: the text gives the aggregate only for (a) and (b) (paragraph (3));
-- where more than one of (a), (b), (c) and (e) applies, this function adds every head that applies.  If none applies, (d) deems the claim
-- to have a value "of up to $1 million", a band and not a number: 1000000 is answered, and the Fourth Schedule is read in its "up to $1 million" column
-- (assumed, not ruled).
-- src:3943 | if the claim is for a liquidated demand, the value of the claim is that specified in the originating process;
-- src:3944 | ( b )
-- src:3945 | if the claim is for unliquidated damages, the value of the claim is that estimated by the party filing the originating process;
-- src:3946 | ( c )
-- src:3947 | if the claim relates to proceedings under the Probate and Administration Act, the value of the claim is the value of the estate;
-- src:3948 | ( d )
-- src:3949 | if the claim does not include any claim mentioned above, the claim is deemed to have a value of up to $1 million;
-- src:3950 | ( e )
-- src:3951 | in the case of a bill of costs, the value of the claim is the total amount claimed in the bill of costs.
-- src:3952 | (3) If the claim is for both liquidated demand and unliquidated damages, the value of the claim is the aggregate value of both claims.
@ref O 25 r 2(2)(a) to (e) and (3) (src:3943-3952)
GIVEN `the claim is for a liquidated demand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value specified in the originating process` IS A NUMBER
      `the claim is for unliquidated damages` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value estimated by the party filing the originating process` IS A NUMBER
      `the claim relates to proceedings under the Probate and Administration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the estate` IS A NUMBER
      `the claim is a bill of costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total amount claimed in the bill of costs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 25 r 2 the value of the claim` MEANS
    IF    (NOT `the claim is for a liquidated demand`)
      AND (NOT `the claim is for unliquidated damages`)
      AND (NOT `the claim relates to proceedings under the Probate and Administration Act`)
      AND (NOT `the claim is a bill of costs`)
    THEN 1000000 -- (d): "deemed to have a value of up to $1 million"
    ELSE (IF `the claim is for a liquidated demand` THEN `the value specified in the originating process` ELSE 0) -- (a)
       PLUS (IF `the claim is for unliquidated damages` THEN `the value estimated by the party filing the originating process` ELSE 0) -- (b)
       PLUS (IF `the claim relates to proceedings under the Probate and Administration Act` THEN `the value of the estate` ELSE 0) -- (c)
       PLUS (IF `the claim is a bill of costs` THEN `the total amount claimed in the bill of costs` ELSE 0) -- (e)

-- src:3954 | (5) The Registrar may, after determining the value of the claim as awarded by the Court, require the parties to pay the difference in the court fees or refund to the parties the excess court fees paid.
@ref O 25 r 2(5) (src:3954)
GIVEN `the Registrar has determined the value of the claim as awarded by the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court fees payable on the value of the claim as awarded` IS A NUMBER
      `the court fees paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 2(5) the Registrar may require the parties to pay the difference in the court fees` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the Registrar has determined the value of the claim as awarded by the Court`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b), "after" read as "where": assumed, see F-ASSUMED): "after determining the value of the claim as awarded by the Court"
        IF `the court fees payable on the value of the claim as awarded` GREATER THAN `the court fees paid` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to require "the difference"; with no difference there is nothing to require

@ref O 25 r 2(5) (src:3954)
GIVEN `the Registrar has determined the value of the claim as awarded by the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court fees payable on the value of the claim as awarded` IS A NUMBER
      `the court fees paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 2(5) the Registrar may refund to the parties the excess court fees paid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the Registrar has determined the value of the claim as awarded by the Court`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b), "after" read as "where": assumed, see F-ASSUMED): "after determining the value of the claim as awarded by the Court"
        IF `the court fees paid` GREATER THAN `the court fees payable on the value of the claim as awarded` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to refund "the excess court fees paid"; with no excess there is nothing to refund

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3 -- Court powers relating to court fees`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 25 r 3(1) order about court fees` IS ONE OF
    `o 25 r 3(1)(a) waive or defer the payment of the whole or any part of court fees`
    `o 25 r 3(1)(b) refund the whole or any part of court fees paid`
    `o 25 r 3(1)(c) order that the whole or any part of court fees be paid by any party or be apportioned among all or any of the parties`
    `o 25 r 3(1) some other order`

-- src:3957 | 3. —(1) The Court may, in any case — ( a )
-- src:3958 | waive or defer the payment of the whole or any part of court fees;
-- src:3959 | ( b )
-- src:3960 | refund the whole or any part of court fees paid; or
-- src:3961 | ( c )
-- src:3962 | order, at any time, that the whole or any part of court fees be paid by any party or be apportioned among all or any of the parties.
@ref O 25 r 3(1) (src:3957-3962)
GIVEN order IS A `o 25 r 3(1) order about court fees`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 3(1) the Court may make this order about court fees` MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN `o 25 r 3(1)(a) waive or defer the payment of the whole or any part of court fees` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 3(1)(b) refund the whole or any part of court fees paid` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 3(1)(c) order that the whole or any part of court fees be paid by any party or be apportioned among all or any of the parties` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 3(1) some other order` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Court may —" names three things

