      `a separate application is made for each unused document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 4(3) a separate application is made for the refund of the fee paid for each unused document` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a refund is sought for the fees paid for more than one unused document`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "Where a refund of the fees paid for more than one unused document is being sought"
        IF `a separate application is made for each unused document` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says a separate application "must be made" and does not say what follows if it is not

-- src:3981 | (4) Where an application under this Rule for the refund of any fee is not approved, the fee paid for the request is not refundable.
@ref O 25 r 4(4) (src:3981)
GIVEN `the application under Rule 4 for the refund of the fee is not approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 4(4) the fee paid for the request is not refundable` MEANS
    IF `the application under Rule 4 for the refund of the fee is not approved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "Where an application under this Rule for the refund of any fee is not approved"; marginal: see NOTES.md

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 5 -- No hearing fee for some proceedings`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 25 r 5 proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `o 25 r 5(a) an action for damages for death or personal injuries`
    `o 25 r 5(b)(i) a cause or matter under the Adoption of Children Act, or an appeal arising from it`
    `o 25 r 5(b)(ii) a cause or matter under the Guardianship of Infants Act, or an appeal arising from it`
    `o 25 r 5(b)(iii) a cause or matter under the Inheritance (Family Provision) Act, or an appeal arising from it`
    `o 25 r 5(b)(iv) a cause or matter under the Maintenance of Parents Act, or an appeal arising from it`
    `o 25 r 5(b)(v) a cause or matter under the Mental Capacity Act, or an appeal arising from it`
    `o 25 r 5(b)(vi) a cause or matter under the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) Act, or an appeal arising from it`
    `o 25 r 5(b)(vii) a cause or matter under the Women's Charter, or an appeal arising from it`
    `o 25 r 5(c) an application for an Order for Review of Detention, or an appeal relating to it`
    `o 25 r 5(d)(i) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Accountants Act in disciplinary proceedings`
    `o 25 r 5(d)(ii) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Architects Act in disciplinary proceedings`
    `o 25 r 5(d)(iii) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Dental Registration Act in disciplinary proceedings`
    `o 25 r 5(d)(iv) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Land Surveyors Act in disciplinary proceedings`
    `o 25 r 5(d)(v) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Legal Profession Act in disciplinary proceedings`
    `o 25 r 5(d)(vi) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Medical Registration Act in disciplinary proceedings`
    `o 25 r 5(d)(vii) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Nurses and Midwives Act in disciplinary proceedings`
    `o 25 r 5(d)(viii) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Pharmacists Registration Act in disciplinary proceedings`
    `o 25 r 5(d)(ix) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Professional Engineers Act in disciplinary proceedings`
    `o 25 r 5 some other proceeding`

