-- src:4018 | Pharmacists Registration Act;
-- src:4019 | (ix)
-- src:4020 | Professional Engineers Act.
@ref O 25 r 5 (src:3983-4020)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `o 25 r 5 proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 5 no hearing fee is payable` MEANS
    CONSIDER proceeding
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(a) an action for damages for death or personal injuries` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(b)(i) a cause or matter under the Adoption of Children Act, or an appeal arising from it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(b)(ii) a cause or matter under the Guardianship of Infants Act, or an appeal arising from it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(b)(iii) a cause or matter under the Inheritance (Family Provision) Act, or an appeal arising from it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(b)(iv) a cause or matter under the Maintenance of Parents Act, or an appeal arising from it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(b)(v) a cause or matter under the Mental Capacity Act, or an appeal arising from it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(b)(vi) a cause or matter under the Mental Health (Care and Treatment) Act, or an appeal arising from it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(b)(vii) a cause or matter under the Women's Charter, or an appeal arising from it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(c) an application for an Order for Review of Detention, or an appeal relating to it` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(d)(i) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Accountants Act in disciplinary proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(d)(ii) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Architects Act in disciplinary proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(d)(iii) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Dental Registration Act in disciplinary proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(d)(iv) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Land Surveyors Act in disciplinary proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(d)(v) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Legal Profession Act in disciplinary proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(d)(vi) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Medical Registration Act in disciplinary proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(d)(vii) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Nurses and Midwives Act in disciplinary proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(d)(viii) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Pharmacists Registration Act in disciplinary proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5(d)(ix) an appeal or application by the regulatory body of a profession constituted under the Professional Engineers Act in disciplinary proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 5 some other proceeding` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rule lists the hearings for which a hearing fee is not payable and does not say that one is payable for any other (Rule 6 says so for winding up)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 6 -- Hearing fee payable for winding up applications`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 25 r 6 entity wound up` IS ONE OF
    `o 25 r 6 a company`
    `o 25 r 6 a limited liability partnership`
    `o 25 r 6 a variable capital company or one of its sub-funds`
    `o 25 r 6 some other entity`

-- src:4022 | 6. Hearing fees are payable in proceedings relating to the winding up of companies, limited liability partnerships or variable capital companies and their sub‑funds where such proceedings are fixed for hearing in open court on special hearing dates, and to appeals relating to such proceedings.
@ref O 25 r 6 (src:4022)
GIVEN entity IS A `o 25 r 6 entity wound up`
      `the proceedings are fixed for hearing in open court on special hearing dates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hearing is of an appeal relating to such proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 6 hearing fees are payable` MEANS
    CONSIDER entity
    WHEN `o 25 r 6 some other entity` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the Rule is about "the winding up of companies, limited liability partnerships or variable capital companies and their sub-funds"
    OTHERWISE
        BRANCH
            IF `the hearing is of an appeal relating to such proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
            IF `the proceedings are fixed for hearing in open court on special hearing dates` THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "where such proceedings are fixed for hearing in open court on special hearing dates, and to appeals relating to such proceedings"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 7 -- Exemption where cause or matter relates to criminal proceedings`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4024 | 7. —(1) Where the Registrar is satisfied that any cause or matter relates to or is predicated upon criminal proceedings affecting the life or liberty of a party, the Registrar may, on the application of that party, issue a certificate of exemption from any fee payable or security for costs required or authorised to be provided under these Rules. (2) An application for a certificate under paragraph (1) must be made by way of a letter addressed to the Registrar stating the grounds on which the application is made together with all necessary supporting documents.
@ref O 25 r 7(1) (src:4024)
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the cause or matter relates to or is predicated upon criminal proceedings affecting the life or liberty of a party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is issued on the application of that party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 7(1) the Registrar may issue a certificate of exemption` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the Registrar is satisfied that the cause or matter relates to or is predicated upon criminal proceedings affecting the life or liberty of a party`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "Where the Registrar is satisfied that any cause or matter relates to or is predicated upon criminal proceedings affecting the life or liberty of a party"
        IF `the certificate is issued on the application of that party` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b), "on the application of" read as "upon": assumed, see F-ASSUMED): "the Registrar may, on the application of that party, issue a certificate"

@ref O 25 r 7(2) (src:4024)
GIVEN `the application is made by letter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter is addressed to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter states the grounds on which the application is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all necessary supporting documents accompany the letter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 7(2) the application for a certificate is made as required` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by letter` AND `the letter is addressed to the Registrar` AND `the letter states the grounds on which the application is made` AND `all necessary supporting documents accompany the letter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says the application "must be made" by letter and does not say what follows if it is not

-- src:4025 | (3) Despite any other provision in these Rules — ( a )
-- src:4026 | no fee is payable; and
-- src:4027 | ( b )
-- src:4028 | no security for costs is required to be provided,
-- src:4029 | by any party in the cause or matter, including any appeal relating to such cause or matter, from the time that a certificate is issued under paragraph (1).
@ref O 25 r 7(3) (src:4025-4029)
GIVEN `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `the date the certificate was issued, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 7(3)(a) no fee is payable by any party in the cause or matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the certificate was issued, if any`
    WHEN JUST issued THEN
        IF `the date asked about` GREATER THAN issued OR `the date asked about` EQUALS issued
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "from the time that a certificate is issued under paragraph (1)"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "from the time that a certificate is issued under paragraph (1)"; none was issued

@ref O 25 r 7(3) (src:4025-4029)
GIVEN `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `the date the certificate was issued, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 7(3)(b) no security for costs is required to be provided by any party in the cause or matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the certificate was issued, if any`
    WHEN JUST issued THEN
        IF `the date asked about` GREATER THAN issued OR `the date asked about` EQUALS issued
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "from the time that a certificate is issued under paragraph (1)"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "from the time that a certificate is issued under paragraph (1)"; none was issued

-- src:4030 | (4) The Registrar may, if he or she thinks fit, refund any fee or part of the fee which has been paid in respect of a cause or matter for which a certificate under paragraph (1) is issued where such fee was paid before the certificate was issued.
@ref O 25 r 7(4) (src:4030)
GIVEN `a certificate under paragraph (1) was issued for the cause or matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee was paid before the certificate was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 7(4) the Registrar may refund the fee or part of the fee` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a certificate under paragraph (1) was issued for the cause or matter`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of a cause or matter for which a certificate under paragraph (1) is issued" is a scope limit with no "only"
        IF `the fee was paid before the certificate was issued` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b)): "where such fee was paid before the certificate was issued"

-- src:4031 | (5) Nothing in this Rule prevents an order for costs from being made by the Court in favour of or against any party in the cause or matter, including any appeal relating to such cause or matter.
@ref O 25 r 7(5) (src:4031)
GIVEN `the order for costs is in favour of or against a party in the cause or matter, including an appeal relating to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 7(5) this Rule prevents the Court from making the order for costs` MEANS
    IF `the order for costs is in favour of or against a party in the cause or matter, including an appeal relating to it`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Rule prevents an order for costs from being made by the Court in favour of or against any party in the cause or matter, including any appeal relating to such cause or matter"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the saving covers an order for costs in the cause or matter and its appeals

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 8 -- Court ADR fees in District Court`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4033 | 8. —(1) Subject to this Rule, a fee of $250 is payable by each party in a case in a District Court for all Court ADR services that are provided in the case. (2) The Court ADR fee is payable when the first Court ADR service to be provided in the case, pursuant to either of the following, is fixed: ( a )
@ref O 25 r 8(1) (src:4033)
`o 25 r 8(1) the Court ADR fee payable by each party for all Court ADR services in the case` MEANS 250

DECLARE `o 25 r 8(3) kind of action` IS ONE OF
    `o 25 r 8(3)(a) a non-injury motor accident action as defined in Order 21, Part 6 of Appendix 1`
    `o 25 r 8(3)(b) an action for damages for death or personal injuries`
    `o 25 r 8(3)(c) an action under the Protection from Harassment Act`
    `o 25 r 8(3)(d) an action under the Community Disputes Resolution Act 2015`
    `o 25 r 8(3) some other action`

-- Fork F-O25-2: paragraph (3) lists four actions "in any of the following" in which no Court ADR fee is payable, and does not say
-- "only".  Two readings.  (1) The four are the exceptions to paragraph (1), which says the fee "is payable by each party in a case in
-- a District Court": an action that is none of the four is one in which paragraph (3) does not say that no fee is payable, so
-- `o 25 r 8(3) no Court ADR fee is payable in the action` answers JUST FALSE for it and paragraph (1) answers JUST TRUE.  (2) The list
-- is a scope limit with no "only" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)), so the paragraph says nothing of another action and answers NOTHING,
-- which paragraph (1) would pass through.  Reading (1) is taken, because under reading (2) an ordinary contract claim in a
-- District Court answered NOTHING instead of "the fee of $250 is payable", which an independent test pass found wrong.  An earlier
-- version of this file took reading (2).
-- src:4037 | (3) No Court ADR fee is payable in any of the following actions: ( a )
-- src:4038 | any non‑injury motor accident action (as defined in Order 21, Part 6 of Appendix 1);
-- src:4039 | ( b )
-- src:4040 | any action for damages for death or personal injuries;
-- src:4041 | ( c )
-- src:4042 | any action under the Protection from Harassment Act;
-- src:4043 | ( d )
-- src:4044 | any action under the Community Disputes Resolution Act 2015.
@ref O 25 r 8(3) (src:4037-4044)
GIVEN action IS A `o 25 r 8(3) kind of action`
      `o 21 the action is a non-injury motor accident action as defined in Order 21, Part 6 of Appendix 1` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 8(3) no Court ADR fee is payable in the action` MEANS
    CONSIDER action
    WHEN `o 25 r 8(3)(a) a non-injury motor accident action as defined in Order 21, Part 6 of Appendix 1` THEN `o 21 the action is a non-injury motor accident action as defined in Order 21, Part 6 of Appendix 1` -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when absent: the definition is in Order 21, Part 6 of Appendix 1, which is not among the sources
    WHEN `o 25 r 8(3)(b) an action for damages for death or personal injuries` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 8(3)(c) an action under the Protection from Harassment Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 8(3)(d) an action under the Community Disputes Resolution Act 2015` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 25 r 8(3) some other action` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (fork F-O25-2, reading (1)): the four actions are the exceptions to paragraph (1); an action that is none of them is not one in which "No Court ADR fee is payable", and paragraph (1) says the fee "is payable by each party in a case in a District Court"

-- src:4033 | 8. —(1) Subject to this Rule, a fee of $250 is payable by each party in a case in a District Court for all Court ADR services that are provided in the case. (2) The Court ADR fee is payable when the first Court ADR service to be provided in the case, pursuant to either of the following, is fixed: ( a )
@ref O 25 r 8(1) (src:4033)
GIVEN level IS A `Court level`
      `the party is a party in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Court ADR services are provided in the case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is an action in which no Court ADR fee is payable under paragraph (3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 8(1) the Court ADR fee is payable by the party` MEANS
    CONSIDER level
    WHEN `District Court` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF (NOT `the party is a party in the case`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "payable by each party in a case"
            IF (NOT `Court ADR services are provided in the case`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for all Court ADR services that are provided in the case"
            IF `the case is an action in which no Court ADR fee is payable under paragraph (3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): paragraph (3), "No Court ADR fee is payable in any of the following actions"
            IF `the case is an action in which no Court ADR fee is payable under paragraph (3)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether paragraph (3) applies is not known, because Order 21, Part 6 of Appendix 1 (non-injury motor accident actions) is outside the sources
            OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- paragraph (1): "A Court ADR fee of $250 is payable by each party in a case in a District Court", and paragraph (3) does not take this action out (an ordinary contract claim, for example)
    WHEN `General Division` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a case in a District Court"
    WHEN `Appellate Division` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a case in a District Court"
    WHEN `Court of Appeal` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a case in a District Court"
    WHEN `Magistrate's Court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a case in a District Court"
    WHEN `Singapore International Commercial Court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a case in a District Court"
    WHEN `Family Division` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a case in a District Court"

@ref O 25 r 8(1) (src:4033)
GIVEN `the number of parties in the case` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 25 r 8(1) the total Court ADR fee payable by the parties in a District Court case` MEANS
    `the number of parties in the case` TIMES `o 25 r 8(1) the Court ADR fee payable by each party for all Court ADR services in the case` -- "payable by each party": the per-party fee for each of them (no exemption is applied here: see `o 25 r 8(1) the Court ADR fee is payable by the party`)

DECLARE `o 25 r 8(2) how the first Court ADR service came to be provided` IS ONE OF
    `o 25 r 8(2)(a) a request made for the Court ADR service by a party in the case`
    `o 25 r 8(2)(b) a referral by the Court or the Registrar`
    `o 25 r 8(2) in some other way`

-- src:4033 | 8. —(1) Subject to this Rule, a fee of $250 is payable by each party in a case in a District Court for all Court ADR services that are provided in the case. (2) The Court ADR fee is payable when the first Court ADR service to be provided in the case, pursuant to either of the following, is fixed: ( a )
-- src:4034 | a request made for the Court ADR service by any party in the case;
-- src:4035 | ( b )
-- src:4036 | a referral by the Court or the Registrar.
@ref O 25 r 8(2) (src:4033-4036)
GIVEN how IS A `o 25 r 8(2) how the first Court ADR service came to be provided`
      `the date the first Court ADR service is fixed` IS A DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 8(2) the Court ADR fee is payable at the date asked about` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `o 25 r 8(2) in some other way` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "pursuant to either of the following"
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the date asked about` GREATER THAN `the date the first Court ADR service is fixed` OR `the date asked about` EQUALS `the date the first Court ADR service is fixed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "payable when the first Court ADR service to be provided in the case ... is fixed"

`o 25 r 8(4) one month` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 1
    `period unit` IS Months
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:4045 | (4) Any party requesting a refund of the whole or any part of the Court ADR fee, pursuant to Rule 3(1), must make a written request to the Registrar within one month after the earlier of the following dates: ( a )
-- src:4046 | the date of a written withdrawal of consent by any party to proceed with any Court ADR service;
-- src:4047 | ( b )
-- src:4048 | the date of settlement or discontinuance of the case.
@ref O 25 r 8(4) (src:4045-4048)
GIVEN `the date of a written withdrawal of consent by a party to proceed with any Court ADR service, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date of settlement or discontinuance of the case, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 25 r 8(4) the earlier of the two dates` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date of a written withdrawal of consent by a party to proceed with any Court ADR service, if any`
    WHEN JUST withdrawal THEN
        CONSIDER `the date of settlement or discontinuance of the case, if any`
        WHEN JUST settled THEN
            IF withdrawal GREATER THAN settled
            THEN JUST settled
            ELSE JUST withdrawal
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST withdrawal
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date of settlement or discontinuance of the case, if any`

@ref O 25 r 8(4) (src:4045)
GIVEN `the request is made in writing to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the request was made` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 8(4) the request for refund of the Court ADR fee is made in writing to the Registrar within one month` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date the request was made` GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a)): "within one month after the earlier of the following dates"
        IF `the request is made in writing to the Registrar` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph says a party "must make a written request to the Registrar" and does not say what follows if it does not

-- src:4049 | (5) In this Rule, “Court ADR fee” means the fee payable under paragraph (1) for Court ADR services.
@ref O 25 r 8(5) (src:4049)
GIVEN `the fee is payable under paragraph (1) for Court ADR services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 25 r 8(5) "Court ADR fee" is the fee payable under paragraph (1) for Court ADR services` MEANS
    IF `the fee is payable under paragraph (1) for Court ADR services`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Court ADR fee” means the fee payable under paragraph (1) for Court ADR services"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The duties of Order 25 as regulative rules`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Each rule says the same thing as the decision function named beside it; the decision functions are asserted
-- and the traces are run (a #TRACE prints a result and counts as no assertion on this binary).

DECLARE `o 25 party` IS ONE OF
    `o 25 the party to the case`
    `o 25 the dissatisfied party`

DECLARE `o 25 act` IS ONE OF
    `o 25 r 8(1) pay the Court ADR fee of $250`
    `o 25 r 3(5) apply by letter to a Judge to review the Registrar's decision`

-- src:4033 | 8. —(1) Subject to this Rule, a fee of $250 is payable by each party in a case in a District Court for all Court ADR services that are provided in the case. (2) The Court ADR fee is payable when the first Court ADR service to be provided in the case, pursuant to either of the following, is fixed: ( a )
@ref O 25 r 8(1) (src:4033)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 25 party` `o 25 act`
`o 25 r 8(1) each party in a District Court case must pay the Court ADR fee` MEANS
    PARTY `o 25 the party to the case`
    MUST `o 25 r 8(1) pay the Court ADR fee of $250`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the party did not pay the Court ADR fee of $250 when the first Court ADR service was fixed"

-- src:3973 | (5) Any party who is dissatisfied with any decision of the Registrar made under this Rule may apply by letter to a Judge to review the decision within 14 days after the decision.
@ref O 25 r 3(5) (src:3973)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `o 25 party` `o 25 act`
`o 25 r 3(5) a dissatisfied party may apply by letter to a Judge within 14 days after the decision` MEANS
    PARTY `o 25 the dissatisfied party`
    MAY `o 25 r 3(5) apply by letter to a Judge to review the Registrar's decision`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
